1
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:17,173
NIKUDAN
(THE HUMAN BULLET)

2
00:00:38,805 --> 00:00:42,104
SECOND DAWN INN

3
00:00:48,481 --> 00:00:51,416
LIFE EXPECTANCY IN JAPAN

4
00:00:51,451 --> 00:00:59,051
IN 1945: MEN: 46.9
IN 1967: MEN: 68.5

5
00:01:00,093 --> 00:01:06,293
WOMEN: 49.6
WOMEN: 72.3

6
00:01:06,833 --> 00:01:09,700
Why do women live longer?

7
00:01:10,737 --> 00:01:13,729
Well, that doesn't matter.

8
00:01:14,841 --> 00:01:19,744
Without war, the human
lifespan is very different.

9
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:22,214
Let's try to subtract.

10
00:01:33,326 --> 00:01:35,123
This is terrific.

11
00:01:35,395 --> 00:01:37,761
A difference of 21. 6 years.

12
00:01:38,298 --> 00:01:42,098
21 years... Wait a minute...

13
00:01:43,369 --> 00:01:45,098
That's surprising.

14
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:47,095
What a coincidence.

15
00:01:47,173 --> 00:01:49,641
No, it fits too well to be a coincidence.

16
00:01:50,376 --> 00:01:51,843
But it's true.

17
00:01:53,346 --> 00:01:55,109
A t the time, he was...

18
00:01:55,415 --> 00:01:58,145
21 years and six months old.

19
00:01:58,384 --> 00:02:01,683
I' m 21 years and six months old now.

20
00:02:03,890 --> 00:02:06,552
This is the end.

21
00:02:21,608 --> 00:02:24,338
You look healthy.

22
00:02:25,445 --> 00:02:27,879
But it's all over for you.

23
00:02:28,248 --> 00:02:31,513
This year, will it be Iwo Jima?

24
00:02:31,618 --> 00:02:33,711
Or perhaps Okinawa?

25
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:36,650
That's what the lady on the beach said.

26
00:02:37,891 --> 00:02:39,825
It's true.

27
00:02:40,426 --> 00:02:43,759
They even captured Okinawa.

28
00:02:44,831 --> 00:02:46,731
Everything is over.

29
00:02:47,367 --> 00:02:52,236
It's as embarrassing as
someone seeing your belly button.

30
00:02:55,608 --> 00:02:58,805
Therefore, it's all over.

31
00:03:23,570 --> 00:03:29,202
What do you think,
ain't it great to be alive?

32
00:03:30,510 --> 00:03:35,504
Actually, you and I are
the only living creatures here.

33
00:03:35,882 --> 00:03:37,372
So let's be friends!

34
00:03:38,451 --> 00:03:41,352
By the way, did you see anything in there?

35
00:03:42,288 --> 00:03:43,585
Really?

36
00:03:43,990 --> 00:03:46,982
You can't see anything in my stomach?

37
00:03:47,393 --> 00:03:49,384
Yeah, true.

38
00:03:49,696 --> 00:03:53,598
The bomb that fell
on Hiroshima is a new kind.

39
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:57,767
Well, according to
the section commanding officer...

40
00:03:58,371 --> 00:04:00,931
Boom! Everything is over!

41
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:06,375
Will Okinawa end up blown away?

42
00:04:06,813 --> 00:04:09,475
Kyushu will be next.

43
00:04:10,350 --> 00:04:11,817
It's all over.

44
00:04:12,652 --> 00:04:15,485
And it's a good thing that it's all over.

45
00:04:16,022 --> 00:04:18,991
Exactly like someone saw our belly buttons.

46
00:04:20,326 --> 00:04:22,624
It's so shameful.

47
00:04:24,297 --> 00:04:25,559
Set fire!

48
00:04:56,396 --> 00:05:00,890
Back then, he never felt shameful.

49
00:05:01,634 --> 00:05:03,761
He wouldn't even blush.

50
00:05:06,639 --> 00:05:10,541
Did everyone get their flints back?

51
00:05:13,846 --> 00:05:17,509
If you forgot your flint
at the bomb site, raise your hand!

52
00:05:20,787 --> 00:05:22,687
You again!

53
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:27,452
Spread your legs!

54
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:29,452
Take off your glasses!

55
00:05:31,397 --> 00:05:32,796
Clench your teeth!

56
00:05:44,844 --> 00:05:46,573
Get up, cadet!

57
00:05:51,851 --> 00:05:53,478
Report your name!

58
00:05:53,686 --> 00:05:54,710
Yes Sir!

59
00:05:54,821 --> 00:05:59,349
Special first-class ground officer cadet
of the pioneer section of land forces,

60
00:05:59,359 --> 00:06:03,386
third squadron of the third division
of the third army, Sakura Taizaku.

61
00:06:04,464 --> 00:06:05,761
Cadet Sakura!

62
00:06:06,632 --> 00:06:09,601
Tell me why you broke
into the food warehouse

63
00:06:09,602 --> 00:06:12,696
during your night watch,
and stole four bags of hardtack?

64
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,598
It was three bags.

65
00:06:15,742 --> 00:06:17,039
Speak up!

66
00:06:18,378 --> 00:06:20,369
I remember that my stomach was empty.

67
00:06:20,513 --> 00:06:22,037
Oh, your stomach was empty?

68
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:24,941
They were eating rats in Guadalcanal!

69
00:06:25,985 --> 00:06:28,681
Give me more details! Why?

70
00:06:29,389 --> 00:06:31,380
That's sort of a long story.

71
00:06:32,892 --> 00:06:34,553
Tell me why!

72
00:06:35,128 --> 00:06:37,892
We cadets changed ourselves into cows.

73
00:06:38,631 --> 00:06:39,655
Cows?

74
00:06:42,602 --> 00:06:46,663
You mean the ones that go "moo," with horns?

75
00:06:46,773 --> 00:06:47,899
Exactly.

76
00:06:48,007 --> 00:06:52,603
All the cadets started to ruminate.

77
00:06:52,612 --> 00:06:54,807
Wait! What is ruminating?

78
00:06:54,914 --> 00:07:00,910
Ruminating means to regurgitate the food
you've swallowed, and then chew it again.

79
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:06,191
A ruminant animal is one who
repeats the operation, such as the cow.

80
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:18,058
Wait, is that kind of thing
technically even possible?

81
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:20,963
If you train a little, it's possible.

82
00:07:21,774 --> 00:07:23,036
I don't believe you.

83
00:07:23,776 --> 00:07:24,936
Show me how!

84
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:26,912
- I'll repeat!
- Permission to repeat!

85
00:07:49,535 --> 00:07:51,867
That was just the hardtack from before.

86
00:07:53,573 --> 00:07:55,234
I don't feel well.

87
00:07:56,175 --> 00:07:58,040
Are you even human?

88
00:07:58,711 --> 00:07:59,973
I am a cow.

89
00:08:00,179 --> 00:08:02,511
I want to become human again.

90
00:08:03,783 --> 00:08:07,981
It may not be a good time,
but may I offer my advice?

91
00:08:08,721 --> 00:08:10,052
Your advice...

92
00:08:11,023 --> 00:08:12,854
Okay, speak!

93
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:15,691
Cadet Sakura at your command!

94
00:08:15,962 --> 00:08:18,522
All the cadets are suffering from hunger.

95
00:08:18,631 --> 00:08:21,498
Two thirds of the rear are malnourished.

96
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:24,265
One third is sick in bed.
One third is absent from training.

97
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:26,636
The last third goes to the infirmary.

98
00:08:26,672 --> 00:08:28,503
If I may talk about myself...

99
00:08:28,541 --> 00:08:31,066
I used to weigh 58 kg before enlistment,

100
00:08:31,110 --> 00:08:32,941
and now, after about half a year,

101
00:08:32,945 --> 00:08:34,936
I've dropped off to 42.5 kg.

102
00:08:35,114 --> 00:08:36,240
The only reason...

103
00:08:36,249 --> 00:08:40,242
The only reason is the
clumsy chewing skills of the cadets!

104
00:08:40,653 --> 00:08:42,143
It's not the army's wages!

105
00:08:42,688 --> 00:08:45,521
The wages and rations are enough!

106
00:08:46,292 --> 00:08:50,058
As the Company Chief declared
during the last company dinner:

107
00:08:50,997 --> 00:08:53,625
Chew 48 times!

108
00:08:54,267 --> 00:08:56,258
When you chew 48 times,

109
00:08:56,269 --> 00:09:01,172
every meal you see appears
to be your own dish of meat.

110
00:09:02,208 --> 00:09:04,301
I will now give you an example.

111
00:09:04,644 --> 00:09:05,872
Start eating!

112
00:09:14,987 --> 00:09:17,785
But two thirds are malnourished,

113
00:09:17,790 --> 00:09:20,691
one third is sick in bed,
one third is absent, one third...

114
00:09:20,693 --> 00:09:21,751
Enough!

115
00:09:23,162 --> 00:09:24,754
What's your point?

116
00:09:24,897 --> 00:09:26,660
This warehouse.

117
00:09:26,666 --> 00:09:27,758
What about it?

118
00:09:28,267 --> 00:09:29,928
There's plenty of food!

119
00:09:30,703 --> 00:09:33,137
These are provisions for the final battle!

120
00:09:33,673 --> 00:09:36,107
The cadets won't
make it to the final battle!

121
00:09:36,809 --> 00:09:38,003
What?

122
00:09:38,811 --> 00:09:41,279
Think about New Guinea! Imphal!

123
00:09:42,715 --> 00:09:46,014
Attu, Leyte, Guam, Saipan!

124
00:09:46,118 --> 00:09:49,178
We all thought about
Iwo Jima and Okinawa in vain.

125
00:09:51,223 --> 00:09:54,351
What the heck?
What the heck?

126
00:09:54,660 --> 00:09:57,595
What the heck?
What the heck?

127
00:09:59,198 --> 00:10:02,861
What the heck are you trying to tell me?

128
00:10:03,869 --> 00:10:04,961
I'm starving.

129
00:10:04,971 --> 00:10:07,269
No! I don't care about your stomach!

130
00:10:07,807 --> 00:10:12,073
I want to hear what you think
about Iwo Jima and Okinawa!

131
00:10:13,713 --> 00:10:15,010
Iwo Jima!

132
00:10:15,314 --> 00:10:16,611
Okinawa!

133
00:10:16,682 --> 00:10:20,015
Then Kyushu, and it'll be over.

134
00:10:20,086 --> 00:10:22,111
So, you want to escape?

135
00:10:22,388 --> 00:10:23,753
No, I don't.

136
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:26,656
There's no escape except to fight.

137
00:10:26,926 --> 00:10:29,861
Japan is an island nation. I'll fight!

138
00:10:30,262 --> 00:10:33,026
But I can't fight on an empty stomach!

139
00:10:33,132 --> 00:10:34,156
Yes you can!

140
00:10:35,134 --> 00:10:38,661
You only need the spirit to
face hardship and deprivation.

141
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,666
You were all incorporated
as Corporals this New Year's.

142
00:10:44,076 --> 00:10:45,907
In April you'll be Sergeants.

143
00:10:46,712 --> 00:10:51,115
In August, you'll undergo the Second
Lieutenant Accelerated Formation Program.

144
00:10:58,257 --> 00:11:02,125
Therefore you must give up Sundays,
holidays, and meeting with civilians.

145
00:11:02,728 --> 00:11:06,164
Sure, the meals probably
aren't enough for a growing man,

146
00:11:06,165 --> 00:11:09,896
but the whole point of this
is to increase your ability

147
00:11:09,902 --> 00:11:13,065
to face hardship and
deprivation very quickly.

148
00:11:15,675 --> 00:11:18,235
The other cadets supported this training.

149
00:11:20,279 --> 00:11:22,679
But you don't support it...

150
00:11:23,149 --> 00:11:24,275
Pig!

151
00:11:24,684 --> 00:11:27,209
- Pig?
- Yes, you're just a pig.

152
00:11:28,988 --> 00:11:31,115
The pig is a symbol of poor character.

153
00:11:35,227 --> 00:11:38,390
That's right, pigs are naked.

154
00:11:39,965 --> 00:11:40,954
You!

155
00:11:42,201 --> 00:11:43,691
Get naked!

156
00:11:45,171 --> 00:11:46,160
Naked?

157
00:11:46,238 --> 00:11:49,207
Yeah. Until special order,
you're forbidden to wear the vest,

158
00:11:49,208 --> 00:11:53,008
trousers, jacket, overcoat, undershirt,
loincloth, socks, boots, or gaiters. Repeat!

159
00:11:53,012 --> 00:11:56,004
Until special order,
Cadet Sakura will not wear the vest,

160
00:11:56,015 --> 00:11:58,813
trousers, jacket,
overcoat, undershirt, socks...

161
00:11:58,818 --> 00:11:59,807
Wait!

162
00:12:00,186 --> 00:12:02,086
You forgot the loincloth!

163
00:12:02,188 --> 00:12:04,452
I won't wear the loincloth,
boots, socks, or gaiters.

164
00:12:04,490 --> 00:12:06,253
Good! Begin!

165
00:12:06,425 --> 00:12:07,858
Um...

166
00:12:09,762 --> 00:12:10,751
What?

167
00:12:11,330 --> 00:12:13,093
What about the glasses?

168
00:12:13,499 --> 00:12:14,830
What's your degree?

169
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:17,266
It's 0.02 and 0.06.

170
00:12:18,471 --> 00:12:19,802
Keep your glasses.

171
00:12:19,872 --> 00:12:22,204
But a pig wearing glasses...

172
00:12:23,008 --> 00:12:24,305
Isn't it inappropriate?

173
00:12:24,310 --> 00:12:25,504
Who cares?

174
00:12:26,245 --> 00:12:29,112
There are one or two pigs
with intellectual faces.

175
00:12:30,049 --> 00:12:31,880
Anyway, you'll be with cows.

176
00:12:31,951 --> 00:12:37,321
If there's one pig wearing glasses
among the cows, it doesn't really matter.

177
00:12:41,460 --> 00:12:43,189
It doesn't matter.

178
00:12:43,462 --> 00:12:45,987
It really doesn't matter.

179
00:12:46,499 --> 00:12:49,491
The cows showed a little bit of
gratitude towards the pig,

180
00:12:50,169 --> 00:12:53,935
because the herd had
increased by a little bit.

181
00:12:55,374 --> 00:12:58,434
So they had a little bit of respect for him.

182
00:12:59,345 --> 00:13:02,940
For example, listen to their compliments...

183
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:07,283
Hey, his dick is pretty big, ain't it?

184
00:13:08,154 --> 00:13:10,179
It doesn 't matter.

185
00:13:10,356 --> 00:13:12,347
No, it really doesn 't.

186
00:13:13,492 --> 00:13:15,824
He didn 't catch a cold.

187
00:13:16,328 --> 00:13:18,421
He was cured of his allergies.

188
00:13:19,198 --> 00:13:24,830
Judging by his face,
he had no time to catch a cold.

189
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:29,473
It doesn 't matter.

190
00:13:29,809 --> 00:13:31,572
No, it really doesn 't.

191
00:13:32,077 --> 00:13:34,978
Until the special order...
Until the special order...

192
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:39,576
And while he was thinking
the special order would never come...

193
00:13:41,220 --> 00:13:43,552
A new kind of bomb was dropped on Hiroshima.

194
00:13:45,591 --> 00:13:47,923
The USSR declared war.

195
00:13:49,562 --> 00:13:52,326
The new bomb was also dropped on Nagasaki.

196
00:13:54,533 --> 00:13:56,967
The special order finally came.

197
00:14:03,175 --> 00:14:07,236
Sir Academy Principal,
it's sinister to shed tears before departure.

198
00:14:08,013 --> 00:14:09,844
Please say something.

199
00:14:13,419 --> 00:14:15,910
What is there to say...

200
00:14:18,624 --> 00:14:24,426
This place once belonged to the
probationary low-officer of the army.

201
00:14:26,899 --> 00:14:30,266
But that's a story of the past.

202
00:14:31,437 --> 00:14:34,167
In short, they're preparing
to dismiss the troops.

203
00:14:36,008 --> 00:14:44,177
Starting today, you, the special first-class
cadet ground officers of the third period,

204
00:14:46,585 --> 00:14:51,079
will go to the final battle
as His Majesty's Holy Shield,

205
00:14:52,391 --> 00:14:57,351
as an anti-tank special unit.

206
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:08,063
Starting today,
you're no longer humans, but gods.

207
00:15:13,345 --> 00:15:20,046
I wish you continued luck in the
fortunes of war, and a good fight.

208
00:15:22,154 --> 00:15:23,519
That's all.

209
00:15:25,224 --> 00:15:26,987
That's all...

210
00:15:32,631 --> 00:15:35,498
Indeed, that really was all.

211
00:15:36,135 --> 00:15:39,036
A man who became a cow, then a pig.

212
00:15:39,171 --> 00:15:44,006
Instead of returning to human form,
he rose to the level of a god.

213
00:15:44,677 --> 00:15:46,235
That's the whole story.

214
00:15:49,381 --> 00:15:53,374
"Is there anything worse than
standing before a crying man?"

215
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:57,389
That's from a kamikaze pilot's last letter.

216
00:15:58,557 --> 00:16:00,582
He probably also felt that way.

217
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:05,222
He would certainly prefer
to be a man instead of a god.

218
00:16:09,234 --> 00:16:13,568
To wish you good luck for
your departure, let's have a toast.

219
00:16:14,340 --> 00:16:15,329
Cheers!

220
00:16:33,058 --> 00:16:35,686
It doesn 't feel so bad to be a god.

221
00:16:36,562 --> 00:16:40,225
Piles of seafood and delicacies,

222
00:16:40,733 --> 00:16:43,167
and a lot of sacred wine.

223
00:16:46,171 --> 00:16:47,536
Do it firmly.

224
00:16:47,706 --> 00:16:49,571
Commander, will we do it together?

225
00:16:50,242 --> 00:16:52,710
Of course, let's die together.

226
00:16:53,312 --> 00:16:55,143
"Really?" He thought.

227
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:57,441
"Well I don 't really care about that. "

228
00:16:58,050 --> 00:17:02,180
"What I really care about
is how to spend my day today. "

229
00:17:03,789 --> 00:17:08,624
"We cadets are getting our first
day off since we entered the army. "

230
00:17:08,794 --> 00:17:14,232
"So we only care about spending
our free time in the best way. "

231
00:17:15,467 --> 00:17:18,402
"We don 't know about the rest.
Only the gods know. "

232
00:17:19,505 --> 00:17:22,372
"Wait a minute! I'm a god too! "

233
00:17:23,308 --> 00:17:26,436
"I'm a god, but I have no idea. "

234
00:17:27,346 --> 00:17:30,110
"Indeed, I've just been promoted. "

235
00:17:31,250 --> 00:17:32,615
"Anyway, let's go. "

236
00:17:47,599 --> 00:17:49,294
It doesn 't matter.

237
00:17:49,368 --> 00:17:51,063
This doesn 't matter either.

238
00:17:53,672 --> 00:17:56,539
This white-haired old man
is old enough to retire.

239
00:17:57,342 --> 00:17:58,434
That's all.

240
00:17:59,311 --> 00:18:02,178
Since he 's retiring,
he 's getting a pension.

241
00:18:02,781 --> 00:18:05,648
But instead of money,
he 's being paid with goods.

242
00:18:06,518 --> 00:18:07,849
That's all.

243
00:18:09,521 --> 00:18:11,216
Three bales of rice,

244
00:18:11,223 --> 00:18:12,747
three bags of flour,

245
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:14,191
three bags of beans,

246
00:18:14,193 --> 00:18:15,421
three bags of sugar,

247
00:18:15,427 --> 00:18:17,622
and a truck.

248
00:18:18,597 --> 00:18:20,292
That's all meaningless.

249
00:18:21,867 --> 00:18:26,304
Whether he makes money from transporting
cargo or selling sweet red-bean soup,

250
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:29,165
it doesn 't really matter at his old age.

251
00:18:29,575 --> 00:18:32,806
This kind of life also exists.
That's the whole story.

252
00:18:33,545 --> 00:18:37,379
SECON DHAN D BOOKS

253
00:19:03,509 --> 00:19:05,374
Is this all?

254
00:19:06,145 --> 00:19:07,908
Yes, that's all, private.

255
00:19:09,248 --> 00:19:11,739
Do you have a thicker one?

256
00:19:12,217 --> 00:19:16,210
One with lots of pages
that I could use as a pillow?

257
00:19:16,421 --> 00:19:18,514
I sure do, private.

258
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:22,923
You do? Please show me.

259
00:19:23,662 --> 00:19:25,527
The phone book, private.

260
00:19:26,265 --> 00:19:28,893
I don't want the phone book.

261
00:19:29,234 --> 00:19:30,758
It's not interesting.

262
00:19:31,737 --> 00:19:35,332
Something more interesting...

263
00:19:36,241 --> 00:19:38,801
But not too interesting.

264
00:19:39,845 --> 00:19:42,609
Something I won't finish in two days.

265
00:19:44,316 --> 00:19:48,252
Something fairly interesting,
but also fairly boring.

266
00:19:48,620 --> 00:19:50,781
Something I can read every day.

267
00:19:51,390 --> 00:19:53,688
I don't know how many days I'll need it.

268
00:19:54,359 --> 00:19:57,487
I've got one.
How about the Holy Book, private?

269
00:19:59,598 --> 00:20:04,399
Holy Book?
You mean... the Bible?

270
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:06,603
Yes, the Bible.

271
00:20:07,272 --> 00:20:11,902
It's hard to read sometimes,
but it's fairly interesting.

272
00:20:12,611 --> 00:20:14,374
Where is it?

273
00:20:25,924 --> 00:20:28,415
Ah, this will make a good pillow.

274
00:20:30,729 --> 00:20:32,287
How much is it?

275
00:20:32,431 --> 00:20:33,796
It's free, private.

276
00:20:34,967 --> 00:20:37,492
- Free?
- Yes, free.

277
00:20:38,303 --> 00:20:42,865
But could I ask you for
a small favor in exchange?

278
00:20:43,875 --> 00:20:45,604
Sure, what is it?

279
00:20:45,744 --> 00:20:47,939
I have no hands.

280
00:20:49,748 --> 00:20:52,444
They were taken by a B-29.

281
00:20:52,551 --> 00:20:55,486
My arms were ripped from my shoulders.

282
00:20:55,854 --> 00:21:00,348
I usually ask my wife,
but unfortunately she's out shopping.

283
00:21:00,792 --> 00:21:04,284
I've been desperately
waiting for someone to come.

284
00:21:04,963 --> 00:21:07,397
Oh, I get it, you need to pee?

285
00:21:07,966 --> 00:21:09,399
Exactly!

286
00:21:14,039 --> 00:21:16,030
Well that's okay.

287
00:21:16,842 --> 00:21:20,642
I haven't laughed so hard for a long time.

288
00:21:20,746 --> 00:21:25,774
Neither have I,
but now I need to go even worse!

289
00:21:26,985 --> 00:21:28,543
Okay, let's go.

290
00:21:30,422 --> 00:21:31,514
Where is it?

291
00:21:31,590 --> 00:21:32,852
Over there.

292
00:21:51,777 --> 00:21:54,746
It feels so good, private.

293
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:58,578
Really? Glad to hear it.

294
00:21:59,685 --> 00:22:01,516
You must not die.

295
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:06,583
If you die, you won't
be able to enjoy this anymore.

296
00:22:08,093 --> 00:22:11,324
That's right, but...

297
00:22:20,539 --> 00:22:23,940
Wow, it lasts so long.
It never seems to stop.

298
00:22:24,943 --> 00:22:27,810
Yes, maybe there's something wrong.

299
00:22:28,347 --> 00:22:31,441
There's nothing wrong.
Everything looks fine.

300
00:22:31,883 --> 00:22:33,373
I guess so.

301
00:22:33,685 --> 00:22:37,781
I trust you would know better than my wife.

302
00:22:38,890 --> 00:22:39,982
Thanks.

303
00:22:40,892 --> 00:22:43,520
Private, what are you...

304
00:22:44,663 --> 00:22:47,393
Ah, it finally stopped.

305
00:22:51,803 --> 00:22:54,135
What are you doing later today?

306
00:22:54,473 --> 00:22:58,569
Whoring around, because I only have
one day to spend as a human being.

307
00:22:58,643 --> 00:23:01,111
Whoring around? How nice!

308
00:23:01,847 --> 00:23:02,973
Really?

309
00:23:03,949 --> 00:23:06,782
It's your first time, isn't it?

310
00:23:07,152 --> 00:23:10,087
You're right.
How did you know?

311
00:23:10,689 --> 00:23:16,650
I can tell because your face
has a look of impatience and anxiety.

312
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:19,124
Oh, yeah?

313
00:23:20,098 --> 00:23:21,656
You're probably right.

314
00:23:22,934 --> 00:23:28,099
My feet and hands are itchy.

315
00:23:28,907 --> 00:23:32,638
Exactly.
I must have been like you back then.

316
00:23:33,044 --> 00:23:37,708
Maybe I was, but that's an old story now.

317
00:23:37,983 --> 00:23:41,146
It goes back to the
end of the Russo-Japanese War.

318
00:23:41,520 --> 00:23:43,818
It's a very old story.

319
00:23:44,556 --> 00:23:47,184
But private, let me just tell you this:

320
00:23:47,759 --> 00:23:49,818
The first time is very important.

321
00:23:50,028 --> 00:23:53,589
You'll either enter Heaven,
or descend to Hell.

322
00:23:54,065 --> 00:23:55,089
How was it?

323
00:23:55,467 --> 00:23:59,062
Like falling headlong.
The shock was so big!

324
00:23:59,738 --> 00:24:04,471
Desolate. I was very desolate indeed.

325
00:24:05,177 --> 00:24:08,635
That girl was as scary as a Deva King.

326
00:24:08,780 --> 00:24:11,772
Although they all
look like the Goddess of Mercy.

327
00:24:11,983 --> 00:24:13,109
Darling...

328
00:24:14,953 --> 00:24:16,079
Yes?

329
00:24:25,697 --> 00:24:27,631
Is he a customer?

330
00:24:28,033 --> 00:24:31,628
Yes, he helped me with that daily thing.

331
00:24:32,571 --> 00:24:34,971
He did?

332
00:24:35,507 --> 00:24:39,876
Thank you so very much.

333
00:24:40,946 --> 00:24:44,211
She's exactly like the Goddess of Mercy!

334
00:24:44,516 --> 00:24:47,815
True. That's the reason
I've lived up until now.

335
00:24:49,988 --> 00:24:51,512
Thank you.

336
00:25:35,033 --> 00:25:36,762
Where the hell are you going?

337
00:25:41,806 --> 00:25:44,604
Ah, I'm going to the brothel.

338
00:25:44,676 --> 00:25:45,802
Where is it?

339
00:25:45,911 --> 00:25:47,003
The brothel?

340
00:25:47,579 --> 00:25:51,106
You bastard! It's the first time
someone has asked me that.

341
00:25:51,550 --> 00:25:53,575
It's my first time as well.

342
00:25:53,985 --> 00:25:57,079
Anyway, today is my first and last day off.

343
00:25:57,322 --> 00:25:58,880
Okay, I'll tell you.

344
00:25:59,658 --> 00:26:00,955
Wait a second.

345
00:26:01,593 --> 00:26:02,958
What's that book?

346
00:26:03,261 --> 00:26:05,058
Is it a foreign book?

347
00:26:05,263 --> 00:26:07,754
It's the Holy Book in Japanese.

348
00:26:07,832 --> 00:26:09,060
The "Horny Book? "

349
00:26:09,968 --> 00:26:13,699
Bastard. Is it your first time for that too?

350
00:26:13,805 --> 00:26:15,898
Huh? Yeah.

351
00:26:15,974 --> 00:26:18,772
It isn't like what's in the manuals.

352
00:26:18,843 --> 00:26:22,904
It's like war. You charge with a
human bullet and let the enemy deal with it.

353
00:26:22,914 --> 00:26:25,212
The enemy who looks
like the Goddess of Mercy?

354
00:26:25,917 --> 00:26:28,351
Goddess of Mercy?
Certainly not!

355
00:26:28,620 --> 00:26:30,144
They're nothing but freaks!

356
00:26:31,323 --> 00:26:33,587
I guess your first time was no good...

357
00:26:33,692 --> 00:26:34,750
What?

358
00:26:34,859 --> 00:26:38,818
I mean, you're telling me
that the first time is important, right?

359
00:26:39,130 --> 00:26:41,655
Exactly! Go for it!

360
00:26:43,335 --> 00:26:46,202
Ah, could you just tell me how to get there?

361
00:26:48,740 --> 00:26:53,803
NEW DEVELOPMENT

362
00:26:58,917 --> 00:27:01,317
- Come here, baby!
- Freak!

363
00:27:09,828 --> 00:27:10,852
What a freak!

364
00:27:33,084 --> 00:27:34,381
What a cutie!

365
00:27:34,819 --> 00:27:35,979
A freak!

366
00:27:36,755 --> 00:27:39,189
Help! Let me go!

367
00:28:08,086 --> 00:28:09,815
They're all freaks!

368
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:18,352
Hey you! Come over here!

369
00:28:36,014 --> 00:28:38,448
SECOND DAWN INN

370
00:28:43,021 --> 00:28:44,318
The Goddess of Mercy!

371
00:28:57,402 --> 00:28:59,097
It really is her.

372
00:28:59,370 --> 00:29:00,428
What?

373
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:04,333
Is that factoring?

374
00:29:04,409 --> 00:29:07,071
Yes, but I can't understand this part.

375
00:29:07,912 --> 00:29:09,004
Do you?

376
00:29:09,114 --> 00:29:11,480
Ah, maybe.

377
00:29:11,816 --> 00:29:12,976
Let's try.

378
00:29:13,184 --> 00:29:16,915
Equals A squared plus two AB...

379
00:29:27,499 --> 00:29:30,297
Plus C, bracket...

380
00:29:30,835 --> 00:29:37,900
Bracket A squared,
plus B squared, plus C squared,

381
00:29:38,476 --> 00:29:46,508
minus BC, minus CA, minus AB, bracket.

382
00:29:47,118 --> 00:29:48,949
That's it!

383
00:29:57,862 --> 00:30:01,821
Um... Is this also a...

384
00:30:03,802 --> 00:30:04,826
Yes.

385
00:30:05,870 --> 00:30:06,894
How much?

386
00:30:07,505 --> 00:30:09,996
For soldiers, four yen and fifty sen.

387
00:30:14,379 --> 00:30:15,812
May I?

388
00:30:16,181 --> 00:30:17,239
Yes, please.

389
00:30:20,919 --> 00:30:21,977
Here.

390
00:30:23,822 --> 00:30:24,948
What's this?

391
00:30:25,056 --> 00:30:27,183
You'll understand soon.

392
00:30:59,424 --> 00:31:01,016
Here's some tea.

393
00:31:01,960 --> 00:31:03,427
Oh, thank you.

394
00:31:07,966 --> 00:31:09,934
Um, money?

395
00:31:11,035 --> 00:31:14,562
I'd like to have the money now.
Please, it's the custom.

396
00:31:33,258 --> 00:31:36,125
Four yen and fifty sen is too much.

397
00:31:38,196 --> 00:31:41,427
It's fine. Money is meant to be spent.

398
00:31:43,301 --> 00:31:44,598
That's what I think.

399
00:31:46,237 --> 00:31:48,262
You could buy another algebra book.

400
00:31:48,506 --> 00:31:50,064
Thank you very much.

401
00:31:51,643 --> 00:31:54,168
Sorry, all the blankets have been burned.

402
00:31:55,280 --> 00:31:56,645
The pillows too.

403
00:32:02,120 --> 00:32:03,280
Wait a minute.

404
00:32:09,060 --> 00:32:10,925
You're... pretty.

405
00:32:28,212 --> 00:32:30,442
"All the blankets have been burned."

406
00:32:31,015 --> 00:32:32,482
"The pillows too."

407
00:34:11,315 --> 00:34:14,716
"Therefore shall a man leave
his father and his mother,"

408
00:34:14,719 --> 00:34:19,418
"and shall cleave unto his wife,
and they shall be one flesh."

409
00:34:19,424 --> 00:34:23,292
"And they were both naked,
Adam and his wife, and were not ashamed."

410
00:34:28,099 --> 00:34:29,293
I see...

411
00:34:38,176 --> 00:34:40,440
Oh boy, a soldier!

412
00:34:40,578 --> 00:34:43,103
I love soldiers!

413
00:34:43,314 --> 00:34:45,179
What's going on?

414
00:34:45,383 --> 00:34:46,714
What's going on?

415
00:34:49,087 --> 00:34:50,645
You're in the wrong room, Ma'am.

416
00:34:50,688 --> 00:34:52,383
Don't call me Ma'am.

417
00:34:53,224 --> 00:34:57,684
This room is for that girl
with the pigtails and school uniform.

418
00:34:58,629 --> 00:35:00,221
School uniform?

419
00:35:00,298 --> 00:35:03,461
No, she's the landlady.

420
00:35:05,436 --> 00:35:06,869
- Landlady?
- Yes.

421
00:35:09,273 --> 00:35:13,573
The boss and his wife
were both killed in an air raid.

422
00:35:15,279 --> 00:35:18,112
The miss now runs the place by herself.

423
00:35:21,319 --> 00:35:23,787
Her only brother died in the war.

424
00:35:26,290 --> 00:35:28,383
She's so brave.

425
00:35:30,328 --> 00:35:34,264
So even though I'm an old bag,
you should just deal with it.

426
00:35:34,832 --> 00:35:37,562
It's all the same anyways.

427
00:35:37,635 --> 00:35:39,762
Really? That's great!

428
00:35:41,639 --> 00:35:44,130
But Ma'am, your apron...

429
00:35:44,575 --> 00:35:47,203
Oh, I was peeling potatoes.

430
00:35:47,478 --> 00:35:49,275
Don't worry about it.

431
00:36:09,534 --> 00:36:12,401
Desolation. This is true desolation.

432
00:36:12,703 --> 00:36:15,467
If you had to picture desolation, it's this.

433
00:36:16,641 --> 00:36:18,336
A freak with an apron.

434
00:36:51,275 --> 00:36:52,742
An apron... can't be a woman!

435
00:36:52,810 --> 00:36:54,607
An apron... can't be a woman!

436
00:36:55,947 --> 00:36:58,814
A white-collared apron
and a mole below the knee...

437
00:36:58,816 --> 00:37:00,477
That can't be a woman!

438
00:37:04,388 --> 00:37:06,982
A soldier with an umbrella.
That can't be a soldier!

439
00:37:08,859 --> 00:37:11,555
I'm a sergeant, a cadet.

440
00:37:14,565 --> 00:37:18,296
You cadets only borrowed
the grade of sergeant, unlike us.

441
00:37:18,836 --> 00:37:20,997
You're just second-class soldiers inside.

442
00:37:21,639 --> 00:37:23,539
What the fuck is that umbrella for?

443
00:37:23,608 --> 00:37:25,633
It's because of the rain...

444
00:37:25,743 --> 00:37:26,903
Bullshit!

445
00:37:28,346 --> 00:37:31,747
The chinks are the only
soldiers in the world with umbrellas.

446
00:37:34,285 --> 00:37:36,276
When will you wankers be promoted?

447
00:37:36,354 --> 00:37:39,289
Next month,
on the first of September.

448
00:37:39,657 --> 00:37:43,559
Japan is doomed if all the
sublieutenants are so textbook like you.

449
00:37:43,694 --> 00:37:44,956
We haven't lost yet.

450
00:37:47,498 --> 00:37:49,728
True, we haven't lost.

451
00:37:50,368 --> 00:37:54,964
I just mean that even if we're winning,
we'll lose if we're led by wankers like you.

452
00:37:55,973 --> 00:37:57,907
I'm not gonna lead anyone.

453
00:37:58,009 --> 00:38:01,035
I'll blow myself up near an enemy M4 tank.

454
00:38:02,013 --> 00:38:03,605
Oh, suicide squad?

455
00:38:04,582 --> 00:38:06,379
The suicide squad are gods!

456
00:38:06,851 --> 00:38:09,979
So you should act like a god
and not use an umbrella.

457
00:38:11,489 --> 00:38:14,617
I'll be a god tomorrow.
Today I'm a human.

458
00:38:15,593 --> 00:38:21,031
That's why I want to hold an umbrella
under the rain like a human.

459
00:38:23,367 --> 00:38:25,699
Can't you forgive such a little thing?

460
00:38:26,804 --> 00:38:28,499
Sure, I forgive you.

461
00:38:28,973 --> 00:38:34,570
Since I forgive you, only use your
umbrella when you get out of my sight.

462
00:38:35,079 --> 00:38:39,311
Well, it would be faster if you
just turned and looked away.

463
00:38:39,417 --> 00:38:41,544
Okay. Like this?

464
00:38:41,652 --> 00:38:43,017
Yes. Bye!

465
00:38:55,633 --> 00:38:56,657
Hey!

466
00:39:01,772 --> 00:39:02,761
Hey!

467
00:39:04,542 --> 00:39:05,668
Honey!

468
00:39:10,915 --> 00:39:12,075
Darling!

469
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:14,443
Honey!

470
00:39:24,628 --> 00:39:26,118
Hiromi!

471
00:39:27,832 --> 00:39:29,424
Here's tobacco...

472
00:39:30,968 --> 00:39:32,367
Rice...

473
00:39:32,737 --> 00:39:33,931
Bean paste...

474
00:39:34,605 --> 00:39:36,630
And this too...

475
00:39:38,409 --> 00:39:42,505
A cubed plus B cubed plus C cubed...

476
00:39:42,613 --> 00:39:45,582
minus three, times ABC...

477
00:39:55,393 --> 00:39:56,883
Equals bracket...

478
00:39:56,961 --> 00:39:59,691
A plus B plus C plus...

479
00:39:59,797 --> 00:40:01,628
bracket, bracket, bracket...

480
00:40:19,583 --> 00:40:20,845
Excuse me.

481
00:40:29,460 --> 00:40:30,620
Thank you.

482
00:40:45,476 --> 00:40:46,636
Is it that?

483
00:40:46,744 --> 00:40:48,644
- Yes, that...
- Okay.

484
00:40:49,914 --> 00:40:51,905
That again...

485
00:41:02,793 --> 00:41:06,627
Bracket A squared plus
B squared plus C squared...

486
00:41:06,630 --> 00:41:08,222
Minus, minus, minus...

487
00:41:08,532 --> 00:41:11,126
Minus BC minus C minus AB...

488
00:41:11,235 --> 00:41:13,760
Bracket, bracket, bracket, bracket...

489
00:41:13,971 --> 00:41:14,995
That's it!

490
00:42:57,641 --> 00:42:58,665
Why?

491
00:43:03,247 --> 00:43:04,737
Where are you going?

492
00:43:37,181 --> 00:43:39,672
A couple and their child died here.

493
00:43:40,351 --> 00:43:44,253
They were smothered like wax dolls.

494
00:43:45,856 --> 00:43:46,880
Your...

495
00:43:49,827 --> 00:43:53,194
My dad, mom, and five year old sister.

496
00:43:56,000 --> 00:43:57,024
And you?

497
00:43:58,402 --> 00:44:00,734
I've been working at a factory.

498
00:44:03,707 --> 00:44:05,902
There's a blanket behind you.

499
00:44:06,810 --> 00:44:08,641
It's dangerous to be wet like you.

500
00:44:08,712 --> 00:44:10,202
You are too.

501
00:44:10,280 --> 00:44:11,770
Can I have it?

502
00:45:15,279 --> 00:45:17,372
Were you born in the year of the rooster?

503
00:45:17,448 --> 00:45:18,779
No.

504
00:45:21,085 --> 00:45:22,109
Why?

505
00:45:22,352 --> 00:45:24,081
You're thin like a rooster.

506
00:45:25,189 --> 00:45:26,451
Year of the rat.

507
00:45:27,191 --> 00:45:29,352
21 years and six months.

508
00:45:29,760 --> 00:45:31,193
I was year of the rabbit.

509
00:45:32,062 --> 00:45:36,192
Rabbit, rabbit...

510
00:45:36,300 --> 00:45:40,737
What did you see that made you jump?

511
00:45:40,971 --> 00:45:43,132
What did the rabbit see that made him jump?

512
00:45:44,007 --> 00:45:45,201
Yes, Mr. Rat?

513
00:45:45,342 --> 00:45:46,468
Yes!

514
00:45:47,411 --> 00:45:50,903
Well... err...

515
00:45:52,850 --> 00:45:53,976
I forgot.

516
00:45:54,017 --> 00:45:55,211
That's naughty.

517
00:45:55,853 --> 00:46:00,187
It was the 15th evening's moon

518
00:46:00,290 --> 00:46:05,023
I saw it and jumped

519
00:46:05,529 --> 00:46:06,894
Bravo!

520
00:46:37,361 --> 00:46:39,454
That's what dying is...

521
00:46:41,398 --> 00:46:43,093
You don't see anything.

522
00:46:43,967 --> 00:46:45,901
You don't hear anything.

523
00:46:48,338 --> 00:46:52,274
Your brother who died at the front,
was he in the army or the navy?

524
00:46:53,110 --> 00:46:54,577
Where did you hear that?

525
00:46:54,878 --> 00:46:56,368
The old lady with the apron.

526
00:46:56,446 --> 00:46:58,004
Old lady?

527
00:47:00,217 --> 00:47:04,347
He was in the army,
but he died on a ship like in the navy.

528
00:47:05,489 --> 00:47:08,583
It was a ship of veneer, for one person.

529
00:47:08,859 --> 00:47:10,292
Like a motorboat?

530
00:47:12,362 --> 00:47:13,522
I see...

531
00:47:14,998 --> 00:47:17,262
In the army, we call it the SS Boat.

532
00:47:17,367 --> 00:47:20,996
The bow is full of explosives,
and it crashes into enemy boats.

533
00:47:26,510 --> 00:47:29,070
A boat for one person must be lonely.

534
00:47:30,280 --> 00:47:31,269
You too?

535
00:47:32,182 --> 00:47:33,274
No.

536
00:47:33,917 --> 00:47:38,081
I'll be alone, carrying explosives
towards the enemy tanks.

537
00:47:39,356 --> 00:47:43,918
I'll dig a foxhole, hide in there,
and wait until the enemy tanks arrive.

538
00:47:44,161 --> 00:47:47,221
With a box of explosives on my shoulders,

539
00:47:47,464 --> 00:47:50,297
I'll run under the enemy tank.

540
00:47:51,368 --> 00:47:53,563
The M4 is pretty solid.

541
00:47:53,871 --> 00:47:56,305
But the metal plate at
the bottom is its weak point.

542
00:47:58,075 --> 00:48:00,168
It doesn't work with a Caterpillar.

543
00:48:00,611 --> 00:48:04,274
If you're underneath it,
it's impossible to run away.

544
00:48:06,884 --> 00:48:09,318
But I'll probably lose my mind by then.

545
00:48:10,554 --> 00:48:13,045
I'll be mindless, but fearless.

546
00:48:13,891 --> 00:48:18,123
I'll wait for days and days in my foxhole.

547
00:48:20,330 --> 00:48:23,925
I'll see the M4 coming!
Closer and closer...

548
00:48:24,167 --> 00:48:26,431
I'll go crazier and crazier.

549
00:48:27,170 --> 00:48:31,334
The M4 is coming!
20 meters, 15 meters, 10 meters...

550
00:48:31,508 --> 00:48:33,203
Now's the time!

551
00:49:35,639 --> 00:49:37,038
Where are you going?

552
00:49:42,145 --> 00:49:43,510
Am I pretty?

553
00:49:44,247 --> 00:49:45,236
Yes.

554
00:49:47,250 --> 00:49:48,478
Very.

555
00:50:25,422 --> 00:50:27,253
Mr. Rat, it's me, Rabbit.

556
00:50:27,257 --> 00:50:28,451
Where are you?

557
00:50:28,458 --> 00:50:31,120
- Private Rabbit, attention!
- Yes, Sir!

558
00:50:31,128 --> 00:50:33,028
- One step forward!
- Yes, Sir!

559
00:50:33,030 --> 00:50:34,554
- Turn to the left!
- Yes, Sir!

560
00:50:34,564 --> 00:50:36,498
- Two steps forward!
- Yes, Sir!

561
00:50:36,500 --> 00:50:38,491
- Turn to the right!
- Yes, Sir!

562
00:50:38,502 --> 00:50:40,402
- Three steps forward!
- Yes, Sir!

563
00:50:41,238 --> 00:50:42,705
The enemy! Duck!

564
00:50:45,742 --> 00:50:48,210
I could die for this!

565
00:50:48,412 --> 00:50:50,175
I could die for you!

566
00:50:50,514 --> 00:50:53,142
I could die to protect you!

567
00:52:45,896 --> 00:52:51,493
Japan is a beautiful country all year long.

568
00:52:51,801 --> 00:52:55,532
Its mountains, rivers,
and oceans make it a beautiful country.

569
00:52:55,906 --> 00:52:59,933
We were born in this great country.

570
00:53:00,443 --> 00:53:06,279
Our fathers and mothers
were also born in this country.

571
00:53:06,550 --> 00:53:12,318
Our grandfathers and grandmothers
were born in this country as well.

572
00:53:12,622 --> 00:53:15,489
Japan is a great country, a pure country.

573
00:53:15,559 --> 00:53:18,460
The only country of the gods in the world.

574
00:53:18,528 --> 00:53:21,361
Japan is a good country, a strong country.

575
00:53:21,431 --> 00:53:23,797
A glorious country that enlightens the world.

576
00:53:52,996 --> 00:53:55,965
Mr. Soldier, are you dead?

577
00:53:58,935 --> 00:54:00,994
Not yet...

578
00:54:02,572 --> 00:54:05,666
But it's as painful as dying.

579
00:54:06,576 --> 00:54:11,275
Then you should go in the sea.
That will relax you.

580
00:54:12,249 --> 00:54:13,910
Really?

581
00:54:28,898 --> 00:54:30,388
It's true.

582
00:54:31,334 --> 00:54:33,029
It feels so good.

583
00:54:47,884 --> 00:54:49,476
Careful! It's a bomb!

584
00:54:55,058 --> 00:54:57,583
Hey, are you alright?

585
00:54:57,927 --> 00:55:00,452
I shouldn't have frightened you.

586
00:55:00,764 --> 00:55:04,427
I wanted to be serious,
but I was careless. Sorry.

587
00:55:05,035 --> 00:55:08,471
Then... is this a fake?

588
00:55:08,571 --> 00:55:09,595
Yes.

589
00:55:10,073 --> 00:55:14,908
The real ones are yellow,
and have some really powerful gunpowder.

590
00:55:16,413 --> 00:55:20,076
But I won't get one until tomorrow,
so I'm practicing with this.

591
00:55:20,350 --> 00:55:21,783
What's inside?

592
00:55:22,385 --> 00:55:23,443
Sand.

593
00:55:23,820 --> 00:55:25,082
Come on!

594
00:55:37,067 --> 00:55:41,868
Hey Mister, are you
guarding this coast all by yourself?

595
00:55:42,038 --> 00:55:43,869
All this by myself?

596
00:55:44,407 --> 00:55:45,999
That's impossible!

597
00:55:46,743 --> 00:55:48,404
I'm not that strong.

598
00:55:48,478 --> 00:55:49,775
How many people then?

599
00:55:49,846 --> 00:55:52,110
Well, just a few.

600
00:55:52,649 --> 00:55:54,742
Wait a second...
You won't tell anyone?

601
00:55:55,485 --> 00:55:57,715
Don't worry, I'm Japanese.

602
00:55:57,721 --> 00:56:00,019
The walls have ears and the doors have eyes.

603
00:56:00,023 --> 00:56:01,615
We're surrounded by spies.

604
00:56:01,958 --> 00:56:03,755
Okay, Okay.

605
00:56:05,628 --> 00:56:08,654
There's almost a hundred of us.

606
00:56:08,998 --> 00:56:11,489
Digging holes and hiding in them.

607
00:56:11,935 --> 00:56:13,800
That's so cool.

608
00:56:13,903 --> 00:56:18,033
So we'll be safe even if
they come with a hundred tanks.

609
00:56:20,410 --> 00:56:22,776
Well, apparently there
should be about that many.

610
00:56:24,013 --> 00:56:25,708
You're so cool, Mister!

611
00:56:25,849 --> 00:56:28,374
No I'm not. I'm normal.

612
00:56:28,685 --> 00:56:30,516
I'm just normal and nothing else.

613
00:56:30,620 --> 00:56:33,384
No, you're great.
You're a human bullet.

614
00:56:33,490 --> 00:56:35,890
Human bullets are great, Mister!

615
00:56:36,025 --> 00:56:37,720
You think so?

616
00:56:37,861 --> 00:56:39,021
Yeah, Mister.

617
00:56:39,162 --> 00:56:41,096
Cut it out with the "Mister!"

618
00:56:41,398 --> 00:56:43,696
I'm still young.
Just call me "bro."

619
00:56:43,800 --> 00:56:46,667
But you've got hair on your legs.

620
00:56:46,770 --> 00:56:48,499
So you're an adult.

621
00:56:49,773 --> 00:56:51,570
You're right.

622
00:56:55,478 --> 00:56:57,878
Do you have a brother?

623
00:56:57,947 --> 00:57:01,747
Yeah. No dad or mom, but a brother.

624
00:57:01,885 --> 00:57:04,183
He's working at a factory in the city.

625
00:57:04,454 --> 00:57:09,619
This world has seen
the rise and fall of many countries.

626
00:57:10,093 --> 00:57:14,553
There was the Greek Empire.
There was the Roman Empire.

627
00:57:16,900 --> 00:57:18,868
Hey, that's his voice.

628
00:57:19,035 --> 00:57:20,662
In China, there was the Han, Tang, and Yuan.

629
00:57:20,670 --> 00:57:23,605
Weird, he's supposed to be in the city.
In China, there was the Han, Tang, and Yuan.

630
00:57:23,606 --> 00:57:24,129
In China, there was the Han, Tang, and Yuan.

631
00:57:24,140 --> 00:57:26,938
Many countries that
were prosperous, then fell.

632
00:57:27,076 --> 00:57:28,737
It really is him!

633
00:57:29,813 --> 00:57:32,611
For thousands of years, there have been

634
00:57:33,116 --> 00:57:38,144
heroes who sacrificed
their lives fighting for their country.

635
00:57:38,154 --> 00:57:40,452
Hey, he's talking about you!

636
00:57:40,890 --> 00:57:45,589
But these heroes disappeared
as soon as their country vanished.

637
00:57:45,728 --> 00:57:49,494
They couldn 't even save their
names when the country vanished.

638
00:57:49,599 --> 00:57:52,591
Japan isn't gonna vanish!

639
00:57:53,203 --> 00:57:57,071
The natural mountains and rivers
didn 't change during this time.

640
00:57:57,173 --> 00:58:00,870
When spring came, the plants still grew.

641
00:58:02,078 --> 00:58:06,071
Brother!

642
00:58:06,983 --> 00:58:12,853
But the people were left with a different
native country than their ancestors had.

643
00:58:12,922 --> 00:58:15,891
From ancient times up until today,

644
00:58:15,892 --> 00:58:21,228
there's been only one country that has
stayed the same, and that is great Japan.

645
00:58:22,065 --> 00:58:24,124
Before the beginning of history,

646
00:58:24,133 --> 00:58:26,624
before history was even a word,

647
00:58:26,636 --> 00:58:28,866
Japan was already the country of the gods.

648
00:58:29,639 --> 00:58:34,269
Ever since Izanagi and Izanami
gave birth to the country,

649
00:58:34,511 --> 00:58:37,878
the great Japan has developed
into a flourishing country.

650
00:58:39,616 --> 00:58:44,747
Now, Japan is fighting against America,
England, and many other countries.

651
00:58:45,121 --> 00:58:49,751
Since December 8, 1942, with the
wise declaration of His Majesty the Emperor,

652
00:58:49,759 --> 00:58:53,126
all of the imperial subjects,
obeying His Majesty's will,

653
00:58:53,129 --> 00:58:56,098
have devoted themselves
to His Greatness with passion.

654
00:58:57,100 --> 00:58:59,193
The Pacific Ocean and the South Seas

655
00:58:59,202 --> 00:59:02,296
have given birth to a new Japan,

656
00:59:02,305 --> 00:59:05,763
just like the Eight Islands
were born in the age of the gods.

657
00:59:05,775 --> 00:59:08,710
This legend has been passed on forever.

658
00:59:09,012 --> 00:59:12,709
As His Majesty the Emperor Jimmu

659
00:59:12,715 --> 00:59:15,548
and His Majesty the Emperor Meiji wished,

660
00:59:15,552 --> 00:59:19,852
the day has come when we may enjoy the
brightness of His Majesty the Emperor Showa.

661
00:59:19,956 --> 00:59:23,289
So we must all do our best

662
00:59:23,293 --> 00:59:25,887
to create a brand new history.

663
00:59:28,231 --> 00:59:32,190
Whoever writes and teaches
these manuals must be crazy.

664
00:59:35,171 --> 00:59:36,638
Got it, you bad student?

665
00:59:36,639 --> 00:59:38,698
Yes, but there's a part I don't understand.

666
00:59:38,975 --> 00:59:40,340
What? Where?

667
00:59:41,144 --> 00:59:45,604
Well Izanagi and Izanami is
such an old story, so I can't tell...

668
00:59:45,682 --> 00:59:47,616
But are the Pacific and South Seas

669
00:59:47,617 --> 00:59:51,053
really the cradle of a new country,
or just some extra pieces?

670
00:59:58,928 --> 01:00:00,589
Bastard!

671
01:00:09,205 --> 01:00:10,968
Who the hell are you?

672
01:00:11,040 --> 01:00:12,098
And you?

673
01:00:12,909 --> 01:00:15,036
- I'm a teacher.
- Just as I thought.

674
01:00:15,144 --> 01:00:16,202
Crazy.

675
01:00:16,679 --> 01:00:17,771
What?

676
01:00:17,914 --> 01:00:19,973
That's not the point.

677
01:00:21,918 --> 01:00:23,112
Why did you hit him?

678
01:00:23,186 --> 01:00:25,347
This little punk ran away from the factory!

679
01:00:27,724 --> 01:00:30,750
Is that true? Why?

680
01:00:31,327 --> 01:00:33,192
I was worried about my brother.

681
01:00:34,163 --> 01:00:35,687
Yeah...

682
01:00:36,399 --> 01:00:40,927
These two boys were left
alone in the world. Can't be helped.

683
01:00:40,937 --> 01:00:43,838
But the factory makes
bullets for machine guns...

684
01:00:43,840 --> 01:00:45,933
Isn't it too late for that?

685
01:00:47,343 --> 01:00:49,208
So why did you hit him?

686
01:00:49,278 --> 01:00:52,839
But it's for the Pacific, the South Seas...

687
01:00:52,849 --> 01:00:54,817
Japan is lost.

688
01:00:55,752 --> 01:01:00,018
We're not building a new country,
just protecting the one we have.

689
01:01:01,324 --> 01:01:03,383
So why did you hit him?

690
01:01:04,861 --> 01:01:07,227
Look, all this blood...

691
01:01:08,865 --> 01:01:10,127
I know...

692
01:01:12,101 --> 01:01:13,898
How much money do you have?

693
01:01:14,937 --> 01:01:16,302
Just a little.

694
01:01:16,939 --> 01:01:20,272
Thanks. For the medical fees.

695
01:01:20,910 --> 01:01:22,377
Look at all that blood.

696
01:01:32,755 --> 01:01:35,087
This should be enough.

697
01:01:35,858 --> 01:01:37,951
Thanks. See ya.

698
01:01:40,229 --> 01:01:43,392
Oh, hurry up and make some bullets.

699
01:01:44,701 --> 01:01:46,965
Are you gonna fight with your bamboo stick?

700
01:01:46,969 --> 01:01:49,335
No... bullets.

701
01:01:51,474 --> 01:01:53,066
Watch out!

702
01:01:53,176 --> 01:01:55,303
There are landmines everywhere!

703
01:02:09,959 --> 01:02:12,792
Everyone's going crazy.

704
01:02:13,429 --> 01:02:17,991
I know I acted like a gangster,
but that's all they understand.

705
01:02:18,935 --> 01:02:21,870
Hurry and see a doctor,
so you don't go deaf.

706
01:02:22,138 --> 01:02:23,366
Thank you.

707
01:02:23,506 --> 01:02:25,736
You're so awesome, Mister!

708
01:02:27,009 --> 01:02:29,204
No I'm not. I'm normal.

709
01:02:29,979 --> 01:02:33,142
My school grades were
even a little below average.

710
01:02:33,216 --> 01:02:36,344
But you defeated the teacher just by talking.

711
01:02:36,419 --> 01:02:38,148
Isn't that above average?

712
01:02:38,921 --> 01:02:41,151
Yeah, maybe. See ya.

713
01:02:41,290 --> 01:02:43,986
Mister! Are there really landmines?

714
01:02:44,894 --> 01:02:48,022
I'll plant them tomorrow,
so keep out after that.

715
01:02:48,097 --> 01:02:49,860
Well, take care you two.

716
01:02:49,966 --> 01:02:52,764
Take care! Goodbye!

717
01:02:59,308 --> 01:03:04,041
ADVANCED COURSE OF
MORAL TRAINING FOR BOYS VOL. 3

718
01:03:04,480 --> 01:03:09,884
That day, he was summoned by his father,
who was a junior high school principal.

719
01:03:10,153 --> 01:03:14,249
Also present was his mother,
who wasn 't much older than he was.

720
01:03:15,258 --> 01:03:18,921
The strict father and the sensual mother.

721
01:03:24,901 --> 01:03:28,132
His father entrusted him with a six-shooter

722
01:03:28,137 --> 01:03:31,868
that belonged to his warrior
ancestors of the Bakumatsu Period.

723
01:03:31,974 --> 01:03:33,441
Die, my son.

724
01:03:33,910 --> 01:03:36,401
Die as the Emperor's Shield.

725
01:03:37,280 --> 01:03:40,443
Let us meet at the Yasukuni Shrine.

726
01:03:42,051 --> 01:03:46,249
His mother squeezed out a tear,

727
01:03:47,190 --> 01:03:50,990
and she squeezed a pimple at the same time.

728
01:03:54,030 --> 01:03:57,329
He bowed, stood up, and started to walk,

729
01:03:57,366 --> 01:04:01,302
then tripped over the border and fell down.

730
01:04:02,538 --> 01:04:04,904
Stop! Thief!

731
01:04:07,243 --> 01:04:09,177
Ma'am! That's dangerous!

732
01:04:18,421 --> 01:04:21,083
Ma'am! That's really dangerous!

733
01:04:22,892 --> 01:04:25,554
Is your pistol broken?

734
01:04:26,529 --> 01:04:29,293
No, my grandfather used it

735
01:04:29,298 --> 01:04:34,235
at 203 Hill during the Russo-Japanese war,
so it should be alright.

736
01:04:35,338 --> 01:04:41,174
Because we're still using the same
kind of bullets in the Type 38 rifle.

737
01:04:41,644 --> 01:04:45,375
But the bullets got wet.

738
01:04:45,882 --> 01:04:47,941
That thing's a hundred years old.

739
01:04:48,251 --> 01:04:52,210
They're a little wet,
but it should still work.

740
01:04:55,124 --> 01:04:58,184
You really frightened me.

741
01:05:07,603 --> 01:05:09,400
What happened to you?

742
01:05:10,239 --> 01:05:13,299
What happened to me?
I should ask what happened to you!

743
01:05:14,644 --> 01:05:17,670
Nothing to be proud of, really...

744
01:05:19,015 --> 01:05:21,347
It's a long story.
Is that okay?

745
01:05:21,651 --> 01:05:24,586
Yes. I have plenty of time.

746
01:05:24,954 --> 01:05:26,148
Really?

747
01:05:28,357 --> 01:05:32,225
Soldier, it's all over.

748
01:05:32,595 --> 01:05:33,653
Yeah.

749
01:05:34,497 --> 01:05:35,691
Probably.

750
01:05:35,998 --> 01:05:39,934
They even captured Okinawa.

751
01:05:40,703 --> 01:05:42,330
It's all over.

752
01:05:43,239 --> 01:05:46,333
It's as embarrassing as
someone seeing your belly button.

753
01:05:51,380 --> 01:05:55,214
Actually, I cook for a group of fishermen.

754
01:05:55,685 --> 01:06:00,679
This afternoon, they said there was
an order to evacuate women and children.

755
01:06:00,957 --> 01:06:02,390
That's it, isn't it?

756
01:06:02,458 --> 01:06:06,053
Doesn't that mean the
Americans will arrive soon?

757
01:06:06,128 --> 01:06:08,028
Ah, who knows?

758
01:06:08,097 --> 01:06:09,257
Doesn't it?

759
01:06:09,332 --> 01:06:13,098
They said that the Americans would
crush the balls of the Japanese men.

760
01:06:13,436 --> 01:06:14,460
Really?

761
01:06:16,439 --> 01:06:18,430
How will they do that?

762
01:06:19,241 --> 01:06:21,971
And what will we do without them?

763
01:06:22,044 --> 01:06:24,103
That doesn't really matter.

764
01:06:24,180 --> 01:06:28,981
They said that the Americans would
take all the Japanese women as mistresses.

765
01:06:29,352 --> 01:06:30,410
Oh.

766
01:06:30,720 --> 01:06:32,347
That's what they said.

767
01:06:36,659 --> 01:06:40,095
I'm horrified just thinking about it.

768
01:06:40,463 --> 01:06:41,987
So you wanted to die?

769
01:06:42,498 --> 01:06:45,558
Yes, but even if I threw myself in the sea,

770
01:06:45,668 --> 01:06:48,193
I'm just too good at swimming.

771
01:06:49,138 --> 01:06:52,335
And there are no trees
to hang myself, just sand.

772
01:06:54,577 --> 01:06:57,273
Then I fell in that hole.

773
01:06:57,480 --> 01:06:58,674
Really?

774
01:07:01,150 --> 01:07:03,118
But you shouldn't die.

775
01:07:03,586 --> 01:07:09,149
When you're alive, even a little thing
like going to the bathroom is enjoyable.

776
01:07:09,592 --> 01:07:11,150
I suppose so.

777
01:07:11,227 --> 01:07:14,060
Well, now that you mention it...

778
01:08:05,815 --> 01:08:12,118
Bracket, X squared
plus X minus 12, bracket...

779
01:08:12,254 --> 01:08:15,781
Bracket, X squared
plus X minus 12, bracket...

