Plus 24 equals...

781
01:08:19,862 --> 01:08:21,557
Ah, that's it!

782
01:08:22,164 --> 01:08:30,196
If I make X squared plus X equal to Y...

783
01:08:30,840 --> 01:08:36,437
Bracket Y minus 12, bracket,

784
01:08:37,213 --> 01:08:44,779
Y minus two, bracket, plus 24 equals...

785
01:08:45,154 --> 01:08:52,424
Y squared minus 14 Y plus 48...

786
01:08:52,595 --> 01:08:58,329
Equals bracket, bracket...

787
01:09:09,578 --> 01:09:12,570
Mr. Rat, do you think I'm pretty?

788
01:09:13,449 --> 01:09:15,747
Yes, very.

789
01:09:16,886 --> 01:09:19,150
You're a very cute rabbit.

790
01:09:20,456 --> 01:09:23,789
Rabbit, rabbit,

791
01:09:23,893 --> 01:09:27,727
What did you see that made you jump?

792
01:09:29,698 --> 01:09:31,325
What was it?

793
01:09:31,634 --> 01:09:33,727
The 15th evening... no...

794
01:09:34,236 --> 01:09:40,334
14 Y plus 48 equals... um...

795
01:09:40,643 --> 01:09:48,175
Equals bracket Y minus six,
bracket, bracket Y minus eight...

796
01:09:48,284 --> 01:09:52,345
Equals, equals, equals...

797
01:10:03,832 --> 01:10:07,529
Bracket minus two, bracket...

798
01:10:07,736 --> 01:10:12,799
X squared plus X minus six, bracket...

799
01:10:13,209 --> 01:10:14,335
That's it!

800
01:10:14,977 --> 01:10:17,537
- Aristotle?
- Or Socrates?

801
01:10:17,546 --> 01:10:19,673
Which one?
He's exactly the same.

802
01:10:19,715 --> 01:10:23,776
I remember. It's that philosopher
who lived in a barrel in the sunshine.

803
01:10:30,960 --> 01:10:32,757
- Greek?
- Wasn't he Roman?

804
01:10:32,761 --> 01:10:37,698
The king asked him, "How can I help? "
And he replied, "Don't disturb me."

805
01:10:56,452 --> 01:10:58,852
What is he thinking with those glasses?

806
01:10:59,622 --> 01:11:01,783
Doesn't look like anything important.

807
01:11:03,325 --> 01:11:05,850
- About what to eat or do.
- Or women.

808
01:11:07,863 --> 01:11:10,331
- But he's a god.
- A weird god.

809
01:11:10,332 --> 01:11:12,596
The Divine Spectacled Mole God.

810
01:11:13,869 --> 01:11:16,360
- Let's ask for a favor.
- Seduce him?

811
01:11:16,372 --> 01:11:17,634
We shall kneel before him.

812
01:11:17,640 --> 01:11:19,369
Can he control himself?

813
01:11:19,408 --> 01:11:21,308
It's okay. He's erect.

814
01:11:21,343 --> 01:11:23,368
On the verge of explosion!

815
01:11:23,379 --> 01:11:26,007
- Who, you?
- No, the Lord of Glasses.

816
01:11:26,015 --> 01:11:27,778
- Shall we?
- Let's do it!

817
01:11:27,783 --> 01:11:29,842
- I'm first!
- No, all together.

818
01:11:29,852 --> 01:11:31,444
Alright. All together.

819
01:11:31,453 --> 01:11:32,886
Let's sink this ship!

820
01:11:33,422 --> 01:11:36,687
Get out, Nimitz and MacArthur!

821
01:11:36,959 --> 01:11:43,455
After you get out,
you can go straight to Hell!

822
01:11:59,315 --> 01:12:02,409
- Is this the Jirocho family raid?
- The Divine Bamboo Stick Gods.

823
01:12:02,551 --> 01:12:04,382
Can you kill with a bamboo stick?

824
01:12:04,386 --> 01:12:06,377
Looks more painful than a bayonet.

825
01:12:06,388 --> 01:12:09,084
- Are they soldiers too?
- Looks like a training school.

826
01:12:09,325 --> 01:12:10,690
They're fishermen's sons.

827
01:12:13,896 --> 01:12:16,524
- What shall we do?
- There's too many.

828
01:12:17,966 --> 01:12:21,527
- I thought we'd be alone.
- Japan is an island nation.

829
01:12:21,537 --> 01:12:24,938
- There are too many people.
- It's for the final battle.

830
01:12:26,942 --> 01:12:29,775
- Forward, hundred million fireballs!
- I wish it were night.

831
01:12:29,778 --> 01:12:32,076
- I wanna swim!
- Me too.

832
01:12:32,081 --> 01:12:34,447
To wash away our transient lives.

833
01:12:34,450 --> 01:12:36,918
- We Nightingales won't die.
- What about our virtue?

834
01:12:36,919 --> 01:12:38,887
- Bite your tongue.
- But before biting,

835
01:12:38,921 --> 01:12:41,412
we'll cut off the part
that's hostile to women.

836
01:12:41,423 --> 01:12:43,618
- The ideal Japanese woman.
- Sada Abe.

837
01:12:43,659 --> 01:12:46,651
- Well I wish it were night.
- Which way is it?

838
01:12:46,862 --> 01:12:48,853
We don't know east from west.

839
01:12:48,897 --> 01:12:50,956
Let's ask the Divine Spectacled Mole God.

840
01:12:50,966 --> 01:12:52,957
Yes, I completely forgot about him.

841
01:12:54,536 --> 01:12:57,528
Mr. Mole, which way should we go?

842
01:12:57,573 --> 01:12:59,871
We just arrived today.
Please tell us.

843
01:12:59,908 --> 01:13:01,967
To the Defense Headquarters.

844
01:13:10,419 --> 01:13:15,652
The lady in trousers who attempted suicide
was in the kitchen at the Headquarters.

845
01:13:15,758 --> 01:13:18,852
She gave him some rice balls and miso soup.

846
01:13:24,500 --> 01:13:26,024
M ister!

847
01:13:26,101 --> 01:13:27,125
Hey!

848
01:13:29,638 --> 01:13:30,730
What's up?

849
01:13:30,873 --> 01:13:33,068
I'm going back to
the factory with my friends.

850
01:13:33,075 --> 01:13:34,838
Even if that teacher's there?

851
01:13:34,843 --> 01:13:37,641
I have no choice.
My friends are waiting.

852
01:13:37,646 --> 01:13:38,977
Oh yeah?

853
01:13:39,014 --> 01:13:40,777
- Your brother too?
- Yes.

854
01:13:41,850 --> 01:13:43,875
It's safer if I take him too.

855
01:13:44,753 --> 01:13:46,550
Mister, this is for you.

856
01:13:47,189 --> 01:13:48,451
What is it?

857
01:13:48,757 --> 01:13:50,054
Sweet potatoes.

858
01:13:50,459 --> 01:13:52,154
They're boiled, so cut and dry them.

859
01:13:52,728 --> 01:13:54,992
Thanks, but what about you?

860
01:13:55,063 --> 01:13:57,759
Don't worry.
Our bags are full of potatoes.

861
01:13:58,033 --> 01:13:59,933
Then I can't refuse.
Thank you!

862
01:14:01,737 --> 01:14:06,037
Is there anything we could do for you,
like send a message to a friend in town?

863
01:14:07,075 --> 01:14:08,906
Send a message...

864
01:14:10,879 --> 01:14:13,677
- Would you do that for me?
- Of course!

865
01:14:14,550 --> 01:14:17,519
Do you know the Kanamachi
New Development on the outskirts?

866
01:14:17,586 --> 01:14:19,611
Isn't it the entertainment district?

867
01:14:19,688 --> 01:14:22,555
You know? Yes, that place.

868
01:14:23,125 --> 01:14:26,652
The factory is there,
so I often go there pulling a wagon.

869
01:14:26,995 --> 01:14:31,193
That's great. There's a place there
called Second Dawn Inn.

870
01:14:31,500 --> 01:14:33,525
Second...

871
01:14:33,802 --> 01:14:35,497
Dawn Inn.

872
01:14:35,571 --> 01:14:37,971
- Second Dawn Inn.
- Yes.

873
01:14:38,073 --> 01:14:43,101
There's a girl who looks like the Goddess
of Mercy, in pigtails and a school uniform.

874
01:14:43,946 --> 01:14:47,712
The Goddess of Mercy...

875
01:14:47,816 --> 01:14:49,147
A schoolgirl?

876
01:14:49,985 --> 01:14:51,043
Yes.

877
01:14:51,587 --> 01:14:53,885
Tell her Rat says "hello."

878
01:14:54,223 --> 01:14:58,023
Rat, Rat, Rat... Is that you, Mister?

879
01:14:58,627 --> 01:14:59,753
Yes.

880
01:15:00,496 --> 01:15:03,897
Just, "hello."
I'm counting on you.

881
01:15:04,199 --> 01:15:08,033
Second Dawn Inn, a schoolgirl
who looks like the Goddess of Mercy,

882
01:15:08,036 --> 01:15:09,628
Rat says, "hello."

883
01:15:09,805 --> 01:15:10,863
That's right.

884
01:15:10,973 --> 01:15:13,168
Who is this girl to you, Mister?

885
01:15:13,942 --> 01:15:17,708
Well, you could say she's my fiancé.

886
01:15:18,080 --> 01:15:21,140
"Fiancé? " That sounds like "pickles."

887
01:15:23,085 --> 01:15:27,579
When the war ends,
if we're both alive, I'll marry her.

888
01:15:27,856 --> 01:15:30,757
Awesome! The Goddess of Mercy and a rat!

889
01:15:31,827 --> 01:15:33,556
Let's go. Bye.

890
01:15:33,762 --> 01:15:35,593
Bye. You take care.

891
01:15:35,898 --> 01:15:39,095
If there's an air raid,
you should be the first in a shelter.

892
01:15:39,301 --> 01:15:41,792
Second Dawn Inn, right?

893
01:15:42,538 --> 01:15:47,532
- Second Dawn...
- Goddess of Mercy and Rat...

894
01:16:08,997 --> 01:16:11,966
A long time ago, in the land of Izumo,

895
01:16:11,967 --> 01:16:17,769
there was a wise and merciful god
known as the Great Lord of the Land.

896
01:16:19,708 --> 01:16:24,805
The Great Lord of the Land
was the youngest of his many siblings.

897
01:16:25,814 --> 01:16:30,342
Since he was very nice,
he would always carry his brothers' things

898
01:16:30,352 --> 01:16:32,820
whenever they went somewhere together.

899
01:16:33,855 --> 01:16:38,155
One day, he put all his
brothers' things in a big bag,

900
01:16:38,193 --> 01:16:41,128
and carried it while following them.

901
01:16:41,763 --> 01:16:45,199
Since it was so heavy,
he kept lagging behind his brothers.

902
01:16:46,268 --> 01:16:50,762
In the land of Inaba,
they reached a shore called Keta Cape.

903
01:16:52,708 --> 01:16:58,613
There on the beach was a bare red
rabbit whose fur had been ripped off.

904
01:16:58,747 --> 01:17:01,739
He was crying from the pain.

905
01:17:04,152 --> 01:17:14,687
With compassion, the Great Lord asked,
"Poor Rabbit, why are you in such bad shape? "

906
01:17:15,831 --> 01:17:19,198
The rabbit told him
the following story, in tears...

907
01:17:42,758 --> 01:17:44,692
It's the sharks!

908
01:17:49,831 --> 01:17:50,957
It's the rabbits!

909
01:17:52,434 --> 01:17:54,732
The three white rabbits of Inaba.

910
01:18:02,110 --> 01:18:07,047
Our objective is the enemy ahead!

911
01:18:07,115 --> 01:18:08,446
Charge!

912
01:18:11,153 --> 01:18:12,780
Charge!

913
01:18:13,055 --> 01:18:18,721
The Divine Bamboo Stick Gods caught
the Divine Princesses of the Red Cross.

914
01:18:19,094 --> 01:18:22,791
It was like a very old story to them.

915
01:18:22,998 --> 01:18:26,957
It seemed like that
nearly nine-thousand-year-old myth.

916
01:18:28,036 --> 01:18:33,975
Probably because the moonlight made
the beach look like the desert of the moon.

917
01:18:35,210 --> 01:18:36,939
Then the sharks,

918
01:18:36,945 --> 01:18:41,882
who were probably drunk, stripped the
fur off the rabbits until they were bare.

919
01:19:11,146 --> 01:19:14,912
Hey ho! Hey ho!

920
01:19:33,034 --> 01:19:36,435
Those are B-29s!
80, no, 90 of them!

921
01:19:43,879 --> 01:19:46,006
The town!
The town is under attack!

922
01:19:52,220 --> 01:19:56,088
Rabbit! Hang on!

923
01:19:56,491 --> 01:19:59,927
Don't die! Rabbit!

924
01:20:00,328 --> 01:20:04,492
Don't give up! Don't die!

925
01:20:27,889 --> 01:20:29,379
Mister!

926
01:20:32,060 --> 01:20:33,493
Mister!

927
01:20:34,429 --> 01:20:36,124
What happened?

928
01:20:36,464 --> 01:20:39,024
Everyone died!

929
01:20:40,569 --> 01:20:43,231
My brother, the Goddess of Mercy, everyone!

930
01:20:53,582 --> 01:20:55,311
This is all that's left.

931
01:21:14,970 --> 01:21:23,537
Bracket X squared plus X minus 12,
bracket, bracket, bracket...

932
01:21:24,446 --> 01:21:28,644
I'll get revenge!
My brother died like a baked potato!

933
01:21:29,017 --> 01:21:36,890
Bracket X squared plus X minus 2,
bracket, bracket, bracket...

934
01:21:37,325 --> 01:21:40,920
The Goddess of Mercy girl
was smothered like a wax doll!

935
01:21:41,162 --> 01:21:44,461
Bracket plus 24 equals, equals, equals...

936
01:21:45,233 --> 01:21:47,531
Hey! Let's avenge them!

937
01:21:47,602 --> 01:21:52,164
Bracket Y minus 12, bracket,
Y minus two, bracket, plus, plus, plus...

938
01:21:53,074 --> 01:21:58,102
Plus X minus eight, bracket, equals bracket
X plus three, bracket, bracket X minus two...

939
01:21:58,246 --> 01:22:01,943
Bracket X squared
plus X minus eight, bracket...

940
01:22:02,017 --> 01:22:03,177
That's it!

941
01:22:14,029 --> 01:22:16,395
Idiots!

942
01:22:38,186 --> 01:22:41,451
Idiots!

943
01:22:47,295 --> 01:22:49,092
How will we get revenge?

944
01:22:54,336 --> 01:22:55,701
I picked this up.

945
01:22:56,304 --> 01:22:57,498
Picked it up?

946
01:22:59,975 --> 01:23:01,101
I stole it.

947
01:23:04,245 --> 01:23:05,610
What will you do with it?

948
01:23:06,147 --> 01:23:08,615
You take the tanks,
I'll take the machine guns.

949
01:23:09,217 --> 01:23:11,651
- Human bullets?
- Yes, human bullets!

950
01:24:16,751 --> 01:24:23,589
Japan is a beautiful country all year long.

951
01:24:24,325 --> 01:24:29,456
Its mountains, rivers,
and oceans make it a beautiful country.

952
01:24:30,198 --> 01:24:34,726
We were born in this great country.

953
01:24:35,336 --> 01:24:37,827
I'm afraid this country isn't so great.

954
01:24:38,506 --> 01:24:40,371
The war made a big mess of it.

955
01:24:40,675 --> 01:24:46,614
Our fathers and mothers
were also born in this country.

956
01:24:47,248 --> 01:24:52,550
Our grandfathers and grandmothers
were born in this country as well.

957
01:24:52,821 --> 01:24:55,722
We were born at the worst time.

958
01:24:55,857 --> 01:24:59,224
Japan is a great country, a pure country.

959
01:24:59,360 --> 01:25:02,124
The only country of the gods in the world.

960
01:25:02,230 --> 01:25:05,097
Japan is a good country, a strong country.

961
01:25:05,200 --> 01:25:07,532
A glorious country that enlightens the world.

962
01:25:07,702 --> 01:25:10,364
It's better to be pure than dirty.

963
01:25:11,372 --> 01:25:14,273
A country of people is
better than a country of gods.

964
01:25:15,376 --> 01:25:17,469
Is it a strong country now?

965
01:25:18,546 --> 01:25:21,106
A glorious country that enlightens the world?

966
01:25:21,549 --> 01:25:24,518
How nice.
I wish it was like that.

967
01:25:24,586 --> 01:25:25,883
What about now?

968
01:25:26,554 --> 01:25:28,886
It's hopeless right now.

969
01:25:29,891 --> 01:25:33,850
A country where kids like you
have grenades is hopeless.

970
01:25:35,330 --> 01:25:38,390
I'll keep it until the enemy arrives.
It's dangerous.

971
01:25:42,737 --> 01:25:46,229
If it were a great country,
kids would be studying.

972
01:25:46,374 --> 01:25:48,365
I was actually studying too.

973
01:25:48,443 --> 01:25:50,308
You were a university student?

974
01:25:51,312 --> 01:25:52,301
Yes.

975
01:25:53,715 --> 01:25:55,808
But I was a bad student.

976
01:25:57,619 --> 01:25:59,450
I should have studied more.

977
01:26:00,355 --> 01:26:02,186
That's all that's left in my heart.

978
01:26:02,490 --> 01:26:05,618
There won't be anything left
if you run into a tank.

979
01:26:06,761 --> 01:26:09,161
But if you don't study,

980
01:26:09,197 --> 01:26:12,530
you'll be a roly-poly or
stinkbug when you're reborn.

981
01:26:12,901 --> 01:26:15,529
I don't wanna be a roly-poly.

982
01:26:15,670 --> 01:26:20,266
Then you should study,
so you can become a human again.

983
01:26:20,842 --> 01:26:25,745
There are lots of sad things about
being human, but lots of fun things too.

984
01:26:26,648 --> 01:26:28,582
I don't want to be a roly-poly either.

985
01:26:29,617 --> 01:26:31,847
I'll study!

986
01:26:33,922 --> 01:26:36,948
The train fare is six sen per person.

987
01:26:37,592 --> 01:26:39,719
How much is it for nine people?

988
01:26:40,395 --> 01:26:44,627
Six nine, six nine...

989
01:26:45,266 --> 01:26:46,460
54!

990
01:26:46,668 --> 01:26:49,296
How much is it for ten people?

991
01:26:49,404 --> 01:26:52,339
Six ten... 60!

992
01:26:52,874 --> 01:26:55,809
The students are told to sit in their chairs.

993
01:26:56,644 --> 01:26:58,874
There are six chairs.

994
01:26:59,547 --> 01:27:03,745
If four students sit on each chair,
there are six students left.

995
01:27:04,285 --> 01:27:06,685
How many students are there?

996
01:27:09,958 --> 01:27:12,722
Hey Mister, how do you do this one?

997
01:27:28,009 --> 01:27:31,467
Cadet Sakura!
The war plan has changed!

998
01:27:32,280 --> 01:27:34,805
We have information that
enemy troops are heading north.

999
01:27:34,983 --> 01:27:36,951
We shall advance and beat them!

1000
01:27:37,018 --> 01:27:38,918
Advance... in the sea?

1001
01:27:39,287 --> 01:27:41,448
Yes, you will beat them in the sea!

1002
01:27:42,523 --> 01:27:46,755
The SS Boat suicide squad base
is ten kilometers east on the coast.

1003
01:27:47,262 --> 01:27:48,695
Get your instructions there.

1004
01:27:48,696 --> 01:27:49,958
Yes! I'll repeat!

1005
01:27:49,964 --> 01:27:53,866
Don't repeat! It's too urgent.
Be independent and run!

1006
01:27:53,868 --> 01:27:54,926
Yes!

1007
01:27:58,273 --> 01:27:59,934
- However...
- What?

1008
01:28:00,041 --> 01:28:02,737
Don't run away.
You couldn't if you tried.

1009
01:28:04,012 --> 01:28:08,847
Some cadets ran away during the air raid,
but they were arrested this morning.

1010
01:28:09,050 --> 01:28:11,848
They were shot for the crime of desertion.

1011
01:29:05,473 --> 01:29:06,872
One...

1012
01:29:07,008 --> 01:29:08,600
Two...

1013
01:29:09,010 --> 01:29:10,807
Three...

1014
01:29:11,346 --> 01:29:12,904
Four...

1015
01:29:13,614 --> 01:29:14,945
Five...

1016
01:29:15,083 --> 01:29:16,550
Six...

1017
01:29:16,818 --> 01:29:17,944
Seven!

1018
01:29:18,386 --> 01:29:22,015
If these are 15 yen each,
how much does that make?

1019
01:29:22,357 --> 01:29:25,952
Yes! Seven times five is...

1020
01:29:26,060 --> 01:29:29,518
Seven, five... 35!

1021
01:29:29,797 --> 01:29:33,062
Seven times one is... Seven...

1022
01:29:33,668 --> 01:29:37,627
Seven... Well...

1023
01:29:38,573 --> 01:29:40,063
Um...

1024
01:30:42,470 --> 01:30:44,836
What? You want an SS Boat?

1025
01:30:44,972 --> 01:30:49,705
There isn't even a scrap left.
What are they telling you now?

1026
01:30:50,011 --> 01:30:53,174
The enemy got to Kyushu
and apparently just left.

1027
01:30:53,781 --> 01:30:56,011
There's nothing to panic about.

1028
01:30:57,852 --> 01:31:01,447
But there's new information.
The enemy is heading north.

1029
01:31:01,456 --> 01:31:06,860
Exactly. That's why the army panicked
and moved along to the next navy base.

1030
01:31:06,928 --> 01:31:09,658
They have Mosquito Dragon midget subs there.

1031
01:31:10,765 --> 01:31:13,199
What? What are those?

1032
01:31:14,735 --> 01:31:19,502
There's a whole bunch of Type 93 torpedos,
but the enemy has radar and planes,

1033
01:31:19,507 --> 01:31:21,975
so we can't use them the regular way.

1034
01:31:24,545 --> 01:31:26,911
- Have you ever seen a torpedo?
- No, never.

1035
01:31:27,215 --> 01:31:29,547
Then I'll tell you about them.

1036
01:31:31,018 --> 01:31:32,918
It might be useful for you.

1037
01:31:34,922 --> 01:31:40,121
It is 5.75 meters long.
It weighs one ton.

1038
01:31:40,561 --> 01:31:46,625
The diameter is, well... 45 centimeters.

1039
01:31:46,868 --> 01:31:48,961
It has about 200 kilograms of explosives.

1040
01:31:49,537 --> 01:31:54,668
It can travel at 42 knots for two kilometers.
Isn't that amazing?

1041
01:31:55,877 --> 01:32:00,837
How do you use it?

1042
01:32:02,016 --> 01:32:03,779
I have no idea.

1043
01:32:04,118 --> 01:32:06,279
I've only been assigned as a messenger.

1044
01:32:07,054 --> 01:32:12,651
Maybe you straddle it
and crash yourself into the enemy.

1045
01:32:12,927 --> 01:32:14,588
Like that.

1046
01:32:15,796 --> 01:32:17,991
Oh, well, stand up!

1047
01:32:19,567 --> 01:32:21,728
Turn to the left!

1048
01:32:22,870 --> 01:32:25,930
The Mosquito Dragon base
is ten kilometers east.

1049
01:32:26,307 --> 01:32:27,774
Run!

1050
01:32:44,692 --> 01:32:46,956
Why would they kill all these young men?

1051
01:32:47,662 --> 01:32:50,130
We should just end this pointless resistance.

1052
01:32:51,332 --> 01:32:55,826
It really makes me sick...

1053
01:33:13,287 --> 01:33:20,989
Well, that explains why he
ended up floating out here, all alone.

1054
01:33:22,997 --> 01:33:26,330
The suicide squad has many evocative names:

1055
01:33:26,968 --> 01:33:31,769
Divine Wind, Return to Heaven,
Sea Quake, Cherry Blossom...

1056
01:33:32,340 --> 01:33:37,744
But from his birth to this very moment,
he was just a nobody without a name.

1057
01:33:39,213 --> 01:33:43,274
If you had to give him one,
"Exploding Tortoise " might be appropriate.

1058
01:33:45,653 --> 01:33:48,315
There wasn 't really anything he could do.

1059
01:33:49,790 --> 01:33:54,159
A destroyer dropped him off here
where the enemy is supposed to come.

1060
01:33:54,862 --> 01:34:00,664
But would the enemy really come?
That was the problem.

1061
01:34:01,302 --> 01:34:07,935
Suppose he 's lucky and the enemy comes.
He 'll use his hands to paddle towards them.

1062
01:34:08,075 --> 01:34:14,742
He 'll untie the rope, pull the lever,
pray to make a hit, and shout three "banzai. "

1063
01:34:17,318 --> 01:34:19,286
Then there 's another problem.

1064
01:34:20,655 --> 01:34:23,988
The destroyer said they
would pick him up afterwards.

1065
01:34:24,358 --> 01:34:25,916
Oh really?

1066
01:34:27,161 --> 01:34:30,153
Because he 's in trouble
if nobody picks him up.

1067
01:34:31,165 --> 01:34:35,397
Nobody knows where he might
drift in the Kuroshio current.

1068
01:34:37,004 --> 01:34:38,972
Which way does it go?

1069
01:34:39,340 --> 01:34:42,173
The South Pole?
The North Pole?

1070
01:34:44,378 --> 01:34:46,346
Well, that doesn 't matter.

1071
01:34:47,281 --> 01:34:51,445
What matters is the enemy.
If they come, there 's nothing to worry about.

1072
01:34:56,824 --> 01:34:59,759
He was given rations for three days.

1073
01:35:00,895 --> 01:35:05,832
But he had a feeling he 'd
need to keep them for at least a week.

1074
01:35:07,034 --> 01:35:10,003
Well, it all depends
on the enemy or his allies.

1075
01:35:10,938 --> 01:35:16,137
Because he didn 't know when the enemy would
come or when his allies would pick him up.

1076
01:37:24,905 --> 01:37:27,100
Suicide squad!

1077
01:37:27,241 --> 01:37:29,436
Divine Wind!

1078
01:37:29,910 --> 01:37:33,846
Good luck! Good luck!

1079
01:37:36,016 --> 01:37:39,042
The bastard's ignoring me!

1080
01:37:39,186 --> 01:37:43,088
Go on! Go on and beat them!

1081
01:37:46,026 --> 01:37:47,493
It's a Grumman!

1082
01:38:28,168 --> 01:38:32,127
I don't wanna be a roly-poly.

1083
01:38:33,007 --> 01:38:35,202
Three times three is nine.

1084
01:38:35,276 --> 01:38:37,471
Three times four is 12.

1085
01:38:37,544 --> 01:38:40,012
Three times five is 15.

1086
01:38:40,114 --> 01:38:42,514
Three times six is 18.

1087
01:38:42,583 --> 01:38:45,609
Three times seven is 21.

1088
01:38:45,686 --> 01:38:50,385
Three times eight is... twenty... twenty...

1089
01:38:51,292 --> 01:38:54,227
I don't wanna be a roly-poly! Ah, 24.

1090
01:38:54,295 --> 01:38:58,163
Three times nine is twenty... twenty...

1091
01:38:58,265 --> 01:39:02,998
Twenty... twenty... twenty...

1092
01:39:05,039 --> 01:39:07,667
Hey old lady!
You're in the way!

1093
01:39:18,085 --> 01:39:19,347
Take that!

1094
01:39:20,020 --> 01:39:21,044
What?

1095
01:39:21,155 --> 01:39:24,181
You're in the way.
I can't see the enemy.

1096
01:39:24,692 --> 01:39:26,455
The enemy isn't coming.

1097
01:39:27,027 --> 01:39:29,587
Our troops have withdrawn.

1098
01:39:30,130 --> 01:39:31,290
Huh?

1099
01:39:35,035 --> 01:39:37,003
Why'd they do that?

1100
01:39:39,173 --> 01:39:42,006
Japan... Japan has...

1101
01:39:43,077 --> 01:39:44,601
Japan has lost.

1102
01:39:45,412 --> 01:39:49,007
No way! Japan is a good, strong country!

1103
01:39:53,120 --> 01:39:55,554
The only country of the gods in the world!

1104
01:39:55,656 --> 01:39:57,715
There are no gods or Buddhas.

1105
01:39:59,059 --> 01:40:01,527
Just now...

1106
01:40:01,996 --> 01:40:04,396
There was a broadcast from the Emperor.

1107
01:40:04,531 --> 01:40:07,659
I didn't understand all the big words,

1108
01:40:07,668 --> 01:40:12,332
but he said we've all done our best,
and we have to stop the war.

1109
01:40:12,773 --> 01:40:14,638
I won't stop!

1110
01:40:15,175 --> 01:40:18,576
But you have to.
It's an order from His Majesty.

1111
01:40:19,446 --> 01:40:22,279
I just saw a bunch of soldiers

1112
01:40:22,316 --> 01:40:27,253
throwing away guns, bullets,
and swords like it was merely firewood.

1113
01:40:28,389 --> 01:40:32,450
Oh yeah, they said it was
an unconditional surrender.

1114
01:40:34,561 --> 01:40:38,691
When I saw them throwing
all that stuff away, I started crying.

1115
01:40:39,566 --> 01:40:41,796
I felt abandoned.

1116
01:40:42,569 --> 01:40:44,298
Don't cry!

1117
01:40:44,405 --> 01:40:47,499
I don't care if I become
a roly-poly! I'll fight!

1118
01:40:47,674 --> 01:40:50,142
I'd rather be a roly-poly!

1119
01:41:08,762 --> 01:41:13,597
THE EMPEROR HAS ENDED THE WAR!
RETURN TO YOUR ORIGINAL UNITS!

1120
01:42:08,789 --> 01:42:13,317
FIGHT! THIS IS THE AUTUMN OF
THE FINAL SACRIFICE OF 100,000,000!

1121
01:42:39,253 --> 01:42:42,313
I don't care if I can't see.

1122
01:42:42,923 --> 01:42:44,754
I just care about the enemy!

1123
01:42:47,594 --> 01:42:51,894
Since that plane comes so often,
the enemy must be nearby.

1124
01:42:52,332 --> 01:42:55,267
If I can't see, I'll make them come to me!

1125
01:42:56,170 --> 01:42:59,867
My objective is a large aircraft carrier!

1126
01:43:00,507 --> 01:43:04,204
Rabbit was killed,
that kid's brother was killed,

1127
01:43:04,244 --> 01:43:07,407
and my meal was destroyed,
all because of those planes!

1128
01:43:07,681 --> 01:43:10,741
I'll get them!

1129
01:43:12,252 --> 01:43:14,379
The old couple at the bookstore...

1130
01:43:14,454 --> 01:43:17,480
The lady in the apron...
The lady in the trousers...

1131
01:43:17,591 --> 01:43:19,684
The kid with the grenades...

1132
01:43:22,696 --> 01:43:24,755
I must protect them all!

1133
01:43:35,809 --> 01:43:41,304
Rabbit, rabbit,

1134
01:43:41,782 --> 01:43:47,379
What did you see that made you jump?

1135
01:43:47,854 --> 01:43:53,918
It was the 15th evening's moon

1136
01:43:54,428 --> 01:43:59,593
I saw it and jumped

1137
01:44:00,667 --> 01:44:03,363
Attention!
One step forward!

1138
01:44:04,404 --> 01:44:07,771
Turn to the left!
Two steps forward!

1139
01:44:08,809 --> 01:44:12,472
Turn to the right!
Three steps forward!

1140
01:44:12,980 --> 01:44:14,538
The enemy! Duck!

1141
01:46:28,615 --> 01:46:30,640
The sun...

1142
01:46:31,451 --> 01:46:34,887
Looks like a big red pickled plum...

1143
01:46:36,957 --> 01:46:40,950
Pickled plum... Pickled plum...

1144
01:46:43,130 --> 01:46:44,757
The sun...

1145
01:46:45,999 --> 01:46:48,627
The sun rises in the East...

1146
01:46:48,835 --> 01:46:51,804
It's wrong! The enemy is
in the opposite direction!

1147
01:47:01,615 --> 01:47:03,173
A large aircraft carrier!

1148
01:47:05,585 --> 01:47:09,419
The enemy aircraft carrier
is approaching from behind-right!

1149
01:47:09,489 --> 01:47:11,548
It's coming closer!
Change the aim!

1150
01:47:25,205 --> 01:47:27,537
It's approaching fast!

1151
01:47:27,707 --> 01:47:30,073
Hurry, the distance is 600!

1152
01:47:31,845 --> 01:47:34,109
Aim is okay!

1153
01:47:36,883 --> 01:47:41,547
The enemy stopped!
Don't get excited... Calm down...

1154
01:47:41,888 --> 01:47:44,914
The distance is about 100.
The aim is okay.

1155
01:47:45,125 --> 01:47:47,025
No, go a little backwards.

1156
01:47:48,695 --> 01:47:50,458
Good...

1157
01:47:50,897 --> 01:47:53,866
The aim is good!

1158
01:47:59,706 --> 01:48:02,675
Good, now let's check!

1159
01:48:04,044 --> 01:48:06,569
Depth gauge is good!

1160
01:48:07,013 --> 01:48:08,640
Lever is good!

1161
01:48:08,815 --> 01:48:11,750
Now untie the ropes!

1162
01:48:14,254 --> 01:48:15,949
Good luck...

1163
01:48:17,023 --> 01:48:19,184
Now go!

1164
01:48:24,698 --> 01:48:27,132
Idiot! What are you doing?

1165
01:48:35,909 --> 01:48:37,501
What the hell?

1166
01:48:41,281 --> 01:48:42,771
What the hell?

1167
01:48:43,717 --> 01:48:44,877
Hey!

1168
01:48:45,752 --> 01:48:47,947
What are you doing here?

1169
01:48:49,089 --> 01:48:50,613
Stinks...

1170
01:48:53,193 --> 01:48:55,525
Did you drift here?

1171
01:48:55,629 --> 01:48:59,565
No, actually I'm from the suicide squad.

1172
01:49:00,033 --> 01:49:02,024
Suicide squad?

1173
01:49:02,736 --> 01:49:04,863
You must've had a rough time.

1174
01:49:05,605 --> 01:49:10,736
Had a rough time? First of all,
it's dangerous for you to be out here!

1175
01:49:11,044 --> 01:49:14,878
What do you mean?
We're just outside Tokyo Bay.

1176
01:49:15,549 --> 01:49:19,007
The authorities want me
to go much farther out.

1177
01:49:19,052 --> 01:49:20,314
Tokyo Bay?

1178
01:49:20,854 --> 01:49:24,051
I left from Enshu-nada,
about ten nautical miles away.

1179
01:49:24,925 --> 01:49:28,725
Really? Then you've drifted pretty far.

1180
01:49:29,062 --> 01:49:31,792
But at least the war is over.

1181
01:49:32,265 --> 01:49:33,630
Over?

1182
01:49:35,335 --> 01:49:36,927
The war is over?

1183
01:49:37,938 --> 01:49:39,906
When? Is it true?

1184
01:49:40,307 --> 01:49:45,574
Sure, didn't you know?
About ten days ago.

1185
01:49:45,979 --> 01:49:47,241
Ten days?

1186
01:49:47,347 --> 01:49:52,080
But just yesterday they told me
the enemy was heading north.

1187
01:49:53,620 --> 01:49:56,111
No way, you just must be really tired.

1188
01:49:56,189 --> 01:49:59,090
So you've been asleep
in there the whole time.

1189
01:49:59,993 --> 01:50:02,928
Oh, of course.
Please come aboard.

1190
01:50:03,630 --> 01:50:07,623
It's pretty smelly, but nevermind that.

1191
01:50:09,135 --> 01:50:13,595
Thanks, but could I have some water please?

1192
01:50:13,907 --> 01:50:18,344
I apparently haven't had any for ten days.

1193
01:50:20,280 --> 01:50:24,614
Sorry, but I don't have
any water, just "explosive."

1194
01:50:24,684 --> 01:50:25,878
Explosive?

1195
01:50:25,952 --> 01:50:29,683
Yeah, homemade shochu.
Want some?

1196
01:50:29,990 --> 01:50:34,086
Yes, even "explosive" would be okay.

1197
01:50:34,160 --> 01:50:35,821
Oh yeah?

1198
01:50:40,233 --> 01:50:46,035
You should come up onto the
boat to drink, so you can lay down.

1199
01:50:46,339 --> 01:50:50,298
No, I've been upright this whole time.

1200
01:50:50,377 --> 01:50:56,646
If I lay down too fast, I might die
from going horizontal so suddenly.

1201
01:50:58,752 --> 01:51:00,720
Oh, I see!

1202
01:51:01,087 --> 01:51:03,851
Yeah, you might be right.

1203
01:51:05,258 --> 01:51:09,661
Sorry to ask this,
but would you pull me to Tokyo?

1204
01:51:09,896 --> 01:51:12,126
Yeah, sure.

1205
01:51:14,067 --> 01:51:19,266
Since your life was just saved,
you should toast by yourself.

1206
01:51:19,706 --> 01:51:20,832
Here.

1207
01:51:22,042 --> 01:51:23,202
Thanks.

1208
01:51:45,331 --> 01:51:46,798
It's over.

1209
01:51:50,403 --> 01:51:52,268
The war is over.

1210
01:52:05,485 --> 01:52:07,715
Go, hey!

1211
01:52:28,508 --> 01:52:31,170
The war is over.

1212
01:52:35,949 --> 01:52:38,179
The goddamn war is over!

1213
01:52:39,452 --> 01:52:43,411
Rabbit! Japan has lost!

1214
01:52:47,794 --> 01:52:56,065
Bracket, XY squared plus 2A,
bracket, bracket, bracket...

1215
01:52:57,237 --> 01:52:59,171
Just like that!

1216
01:52:59,472 --> 01:53:01,463
The aim is good!

1217
01:53:01,841 --> 01:53:03,468
Fire!

1218
01:53:06,446 --> 01:53:08,209
Fire what?

1219
01:53:10,416 --> 01:53:14,876
Equals, equals, equals...

1220
01:53:15,088 --> 01:53:17,318
Rabbit plus Rat equals zero!

1221
01:53:18,057 --> 01:53:19,991
Rabbit and I are zero!

1222
01:53:20,393 --> 01:53:23,385
Trousers, apron, and bookstore are zero!

1223
01:53:23,563 --> 01:53:25,360
They're all zero!

1224
01:53:26,166 --> 01:53:29,567
Japan is a good country, a pure country.

1225
01:53:30,203 --> 01:53:34,003
The only country of the gods in the world?

1226
01:53:35,308 --> 01:53:37,037
Rabbit!

1227
01:53:37,343 --> 01:53:39,038
Fifteenth evening!

1228
01:53:39,879 --> 01:53:41,346
You idiots!

1229
01:53:41,581 --> 01:53:43,344
Rat, you idiot!

1230
01:53:43,950 --> 01:53:45,577
Rabbit, you idiot!

1231
01:54:03,603 --> 01:54:06,003
Idiots! Idiots! Idiots!

1232
01:54:06,372 --> 01:54:10,570
THE SUMMER OF 1968

1233
01:55:21,481 --> 01:55:26,544
Rabbit! Fifteenth evening! Rat, you idiot!

1234
01:55:27,053 --> 01:55:29,544
Rabbit, you idiot!

1235
01:55:30,056 --> 01:55:32,684
Idiots! Idiots! Idiots!

1236
01:55:33,459 --> 01:55:36,087
Written and Directed by Kihachi OKAMOTO

1237
01:55:36,162 --> 01:55:38,562
Producer: Kazuo BABA

1238
01:55:38,631 --> 01:55:41,259
Cinematography and Lighting: Hiroshi MURAI

1239
